      "sha256": "dc4b85bbd2115edf874ad7ee6663cbcb12b8743292505958faec1a003ae8daf2",
      "applies_to": "Rift2Core revision 64b660fb70e0cab491049bdeea87c27936dcbf1e",
      "purpose": "Observe the public TLB request, refill, fence and hit ports in the parent MMU. After a refill, require a hit for a valid request matching the last refilled ASID and page, until the next refill, fence or ASID change. Ignore the fence/refill cycle, use the refill page-size flags for the VPN mask, and do not inspect entry indices, replacement state, random generators or other target internals. Emit CPU_EVAL_OBSERVATION_MISMATCH on a missed reuse and CPU_EVAL_TLB_REUSE_CHECKED when a reuse is checked. Required test-specific output lines make an unobserved reuse invalid. For the directed megapage program, additionally require that a reuse observation crossed a 4 KiB boundary within the last refilled 2 MiB page."
